  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $2$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $2:3.$",
